From 4e2eaba8332fb6ed749a5e51e298f3562400f874 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 10:19:42 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] dns: remove the EDNS Client Subnet option

Owner decision. The switch is gone from the DNS Failover page, the
add-subnet emitter from start_dnsmasq(), the reaper_dns_ecs default from
defaults.c, and the four dict tokens from all 25 languages.

Removed at the root rather than hidden: taking the control out while
leaving the emitter would have stranded any box with reaper_dns_ecs=1
with ECS permanently ON and no way to turn it off - the exact exposure
the removal is for.

What settled it. EDNS Client Subnet carried the FULL client address, and
nothing it bought covered that. AdGuard Home only LOGS the value and
never matches rules on it (asked upstream twice and declined -
AdGuardHome #4383, #6104), so per-client rules on an AdGuard target
stayed inert however the switch was set. And dnsmasq attaches the option
at RECEIVE time, before upstream selection, so a failover to a public
resolver carried the client's address out of the network with nothing in
the path able to strip it.

The reasoning is kept in the source beside the no-cache switch, which
shares that comment block, so anyone tempted to add it back reads first:
it would need a per-upstream strip at dnsmasq's server_send().

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
